sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch11-20> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch11-20--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch11-20--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on wolfram2002-ch11-20: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.81" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.813"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    dct:type "resolution-route/proof" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.8"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "For rules 90 and 150 the state at dyadic times is an explicit linear function of the initial condition, a fact proved in the additive-cellular-automaton literature and easy to recompute. Behaviors that do not collapse in that way cannot occur, so those rules are not universal. The wider nested class is settled in the same way once nested is identified with a substitution or linear schema, which is the argument the book gives." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: For additive rules such as 90 and 150, use the linear representation over the field with two elements and check that the configuration at 2^k steps is a fixed superposition of shifts of the initial condition. Confirm non-universality because some computable spacetime diagrams never return to that form; refute it by exhibiting a universal computation inside an additive rule." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "The algebraic proof covers linear rules directly; purely nested but nonlinear rules need a separate definition of nested before the same conclusion applies." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch11-20--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch11-20--grok--dataset-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch11-20--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of wolfram2002-ch11-20 by Grok 4.7: 0.8" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.8"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch11-20--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch11-20> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch11-20--grok--operationalizability> .
